        "content": "<p>Some <code>simp</code> lemmas of the form <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subring.toSubsemiring_top#doc\">docs#Subring.toSubsemiring_top</a> are missing: eg <code>Subsemiring.toSubmonoid_top</code>.</p>\n<p>I could PR the ones I need, but this feels unsustainable and hard to maintain. Is there a structure that gives us the <code>simp</code> lemmas we want automatically? It's not <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LatticeHom#doc\">docs#LatticeHom</a> because we don't preserve joins.</p>",
        "id": 614086165,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1785602950
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>is it a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=sInfHom#doc\">docs#sInfHom</a></p>",
